From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] shaders: 16-bit types in shader inputs and outputs only where the device has storageInputOutput16

DxvkDevice sets Supports16BitArithmetic on shaderFloat16 alone, and the
shader compiler then lowers min-precision types to 16-bit ones in shader
inputs and outputs too, which needs storageInputOutput16. A device with
16-bit arithmetic but no 16-bit I/O (Intel gen 9 with ANV, a UHD 630 on
Mesa 26.0.8) runs such shaders with a feature it does not have: the result
is undefined, and Direct2D's glyph shader draws noise or nothing, so
DirectWrite text, font icons and the boot spinner are garbled while GDI text
is clean. The flag now needs both features, and storageInputOutput16 is
requested where the device has it. Devices with both (Radeon) keep 16-bit
types. The SPIR-V side, the capability on the I/O variables, is
dxvk-patches/dxbc-spirv/0001.
---
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device.cpp
index 02218254..f8b591a7 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device.cpp
@@ -765,7 +765,11 @@ namespace dxvk {
     m_shaderOptions.minStorageBufferAlignment =
       m_properties.core.properties.limits.minStorageBufferOffsetAlignment;
 
-    if (m_features.vk12.shaderFloat16)
+    // Min-precision types become 16-bit ones in shader inputs and outputs too,
+    // which takes storageInputOutput16: a device with 16-bit arithmetic but no
+    // 16-bit I/O (Intel gen 9) keeps 32-bit types, or its shaders use a feature
+    // it does not have (Direct2D's glyph shader draws noise on a UHD 630).
+    if (m_features.vk12.shaderFloat16 && m_features.vk11.storageInputOutput16)
       m_shaderOptions.flags.set(DxvkShaderCompileFlag::Supports16BitArithmetic);
 
     if (m_features.vk11.storagePushConstant16 && m_features.vk12.storagePushConstant8)
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
index 60ce074d..854ffb42 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
@@ -877,6 +877,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
       ENABLE_FEATURE(vk11, shaderDrawParameters, true),
       ENABLE_FEATURE(vk11, storageBuffer16BitAccess, true),
+      ENABLE_FEATURE(vk11, storageInputOutput16, false),
       ENABLE_FEATURE(vk11, storagePushConstant16, false),
 
       ENABLE_FEATURE(vk12, bufferDeviceAddress, true),
